Here is the structured goal model based on the mission description:

### Goal Model Summary

#### Goals

| Goal ID | Goal Title | Goal Text | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation | Justification |
|--------|------------|-----------|--------------------|-----------|----------|---------------|
| G1     | Collect and Deliver Resources | Ensure all required resources are collected from storage and delivered to the specified location. | # (Parallel) | Achieve | - | Mission requires multiple robots to handle different resources independently in parallel. |

#### Sub-Goals of G1

| Goal ID | Goal Title | Goal Text | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation | Justification |
|--------|------------|-----------|--------------------|-----------|----------|---------------|
| G2     | Deliver Resource A | Collect and deliver Resource A to the specified location. | ; (Sequential) | Achieve | AND | Both collection and delivery must occur for successful delivery. |
| G3     | Deliver Resource B | Collect and deliver Resource B to the specified location. | ; (Sequential) | Achieve | AND | Both collection and delivery must occur for successful delivery. |
| G4     | Deliver Resource C | Collect and deliver Resource C to the specified location. | ; (Sequential) | Achieve | AND | Both collection and delivery must occur for successful delivery. |

#### Sub-Goals of G2

| Goal ID | Goal Title | Goal Text | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation | Justification |
|--------|------------|-----------|--------------------|-----------|----------|---------------|
| G2.1   | Collection Phase | Collect Resource A from storage. | FALLBACK(G2.1a, G2.1b) | Achieve | AND | If battery drops to 10%, the robot must recharge before continuing. |
| G2.2   | Delivery Phase | Deliver Resource A to the specified location. | FALLBACK(G2.2a, G2.2b) | Achieve | AND | If battery drops to 30%, the robot must return to a checkpoint and another robot takes over. |

#### Tasks

| Task ID | Task Title | Task Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots | Justification |
|---------|------------|-----------|----------|----------|-------------------|---------------|
| AT2.1   | Collect Resource A | Go to storage and collect Resource A. | - | Storage Location | 1 | Single robot assigned to collect resource A. |
| AT2.2   | Deliver Resource A | Transport Resource A to the specified location. | - | Delivery Location | 1 | Single robot assigned to deliver resource A. |
| AT2.1a  | Recharge Robot | Recharge the robot at the recharging station. | - | Recharging Station | 1 | Required if battery drops to 10%. |
| AT2.1b  | Continue Collection | Resume collection after recharging. | - | Storage Location | 1 | Continue after recharging. |
| AT2.2a  | Continue Delivery | Resume delivery after recharging. | - | Delivery Location | 1 | Continue after recharging. |
| AT2.2b  | Return to Checkpoint | Return Resource A to the checkpoint. | - | Checkpoint | 1 | If delivery cannot be completed, return to checkpoint. |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G3, G4 [AND]**: All resources must be delivered for the mission to succeed. Each resource delivery is an AND condition because they all need to be completed, but their execution can be parallelized.

- **G2 -> G2.1, G2.2 [AND]**: Both collection and delivery phases must be completed for Resource A.

- **G2.1 -> AT2.1 [AND]**: The collection phase must be executed by a single robot.

- **G2.1 -> AT2.1a, AT2.1b [FALLBACK]**: If the robot's battery drops to 10%, it must recharge (AT2.1a) before continuing (AT2.1b).

- **G2.2 -> AT2.2 [AND]**: The delivery phase must be executed by a single robot.

- **G2.2 -> AT2.2a, AT2.2b [FALLBACK]**: If the robot's battery drops to 30%, it must return to the checkpoint (AT2.2a) and let another robot take over (AT2.2b).

This model ensures that each resource is handled independently and efficiently, with fallback mechanisms in place for battery management.
